ANNOUNCER: Congratulations.

04:37:39.560 --> 04:37:41.360
It's now my pleasure
to introduce

04:37:41.360 --> 04:37:45.079
Paula J. Olsiewski
the Chief Marshal,

04:37:45.079 --> 04:37:48.110
who will greet the graduates.

04:37:48.110 --> 04:37:52.880
Dr. Olsiewski is a member
of the class of 1979

04:37:52.880 --> 04:37:55.729
and is currently serving as the
president of the Association

04:37:55.729 --> 04:37:59.822
of Alumni and Alumnae of MIT.

04:37:59.822 --> 04:38:00.322
Paula?

04:38:05.719 --> 04:38:07.950
OLSIEWSKI: Thank you, Dana.

04:38:07.950 --> 04:38:11.970
It is my great honor to
recognize the distinguished

04:38:11.970 --> 04:38:21.126
members of the 50th-year
reunion Class of 1954--

04:38:21.126 --> 04:38:24.570
[APPLAUSE]

04:38:32.950 --> 04:38:39.676
--and their very special
class president and dear

04:38:39.676 --> 04:38:43.389
mentor of mine, Paul Gray.

04:38:43.389 --> 04:38:46.854
[APPLAUSE]

04:38:53.310 --> 04:38:57.349
This is the first
time in 44 years

04:38:57.349 --> 04:38:59.960
that Paul has not
been on this stage

04:38:59.960 --> 04:39:05.200
during commencement as either
a participating faculty member,

04:39:05.200 --> 04:39:09.184
chancellor, president,
or chairman.

04:39:09.184 --> 04:39:13.096
Congratulations on
your reunion, Paul.

04:39:13.096 --> 04:39:16.519
[APPLAUSE]

04:39:18.970 --> 04:39:23.439
Now I invite the class
of 1954 to join me

04:39:23.439 --> 04:39:28.230
in congratulating all
of the 2004 graduates

04:39:28.230 --> 04:39:31.627
and officially welcoming
you into the alumni

04:39:31.627 --> 04:39:36.487
family, your infinite
connection to MIT.

04:39:36.487 --> 04:39:39.889
[APPLAUSE]

04:39:46.700 --> 04:39:49.230
PRESENTER: Thank you, Paula.

04:39:49.230 --> 04:39:55.110
The 138th Commencement exercises
of the Massachusetts Institute

04:39:55.110 --> 04:39:59.178
of Technology are now concluded.

04:39:59.178 --> 04:40:02.094
[CHEERS AND APPLAUSE]

04:40:06.954 --> 04:40:13.340
A reception will follow on
Kresge Oval in the West Campus

04:40:13.340 --> 04:40:14.780
plaza.

04:40:14.780 --> 04:40:16.340
And the audience
and graduates are

04:40:16.340 --> 04:40:19.220
requested to remain
at their seats

04:40:19.220 --> 04:40:22.880
until the stage
assembly has recessed.

04:40:22.880 --> 04:40:26.800
And now please join
the MIT Chorallaries

04:40:26.800 --> 04:40:28.754
in singing the school song.

04:40:36.224 --> 04:40:39.710
[MUSIC - CHORALLARIES, "ARISE
 ALL YE OF MIT"]

04:40:47.180 --> 04:40:56.823
(SINGING) Arise all ye of
MIT, in loyal fellowship.

04:40:59.769 --> 04:41:12.156
The future beckons unto thee,
and life is full and rich.

04:41:12.156 --> 04:41:18.108
Arise and raise
your glass up high;

04:41:18.108 --> 04:41:27.058
tonight shall ever
be a memory that

04:41:27.058 --> 04:41:32.832
will never die, for ye of MIT.

04:41:36.290 --> 04:41:48.828
Thy sons and daughters, MIT,
return from far and wide

04:41:48.828 --> 04:42:00.647
and gather here once more to
be re-nourished by thy side.

04:42:00.647 --> 04:42:12.999
And as we raise our glasses high
to pledge our love for thee,

04:42:12.999 --> 04:42:21.396
we join all those of days
gone by in praise of MIT.

04:42:24.612 --> 04:42:26.570
[MUSIC - CHORALLARIES, "TAKE ME
 BACK TO TECH"]

04:42:26.570 --> 04:42:31.940
(SINGING) Oh, I wish that I were
back again at Tech on Boylston

04:42:31.940 --> 04:42:36.770
Street, dressed in my dinky
uniform so dapper and so neat.

04:42:36.770 --> 04:42:40.040
I'm crazy after calculus;
I never had enough;

04:42:40.040 --> 04:42:41.940
t'was hard to be
dragged away so young,

04:42:41.940 --> 04:42:43.590
it was horribly awfully tough.

04:42:43.590 --> 04:42:47.875
Hurrah for technology,
'ology, 'ology, oh,

04:42:47.875 --> 04:42:51.790
glorious old technology,
'ology, 'ology, oh.

04:42:51.790 --> 04:42:53.570
Back in the days that
were free from care

04:42:53.570 --> 04:42:56.090
in the 'ology varsity
shop, with nothing

04:42:56.090 --> 04:42:58.716
to do but to analyze air
in an anemometrical top.

04:42:58.716 --> 04:43:02.700
The differentiation of
the trigonmetric powers,

04:43:02.700 --> 04:43:04.648
the constant pi
that made me sigh

04:43:04.648 --> 04:43:06.216
in those happy days of ours.

04:43:06.216 --> 04:43:10.700
Hurrah for technology,
'ology, 'ology, oh.

04:43:10.700 --> 04:43:14.300
Oh, glorious old technology,
'ology, 'ology, oh.

04:43:14.300 --> 04:43:16.000
Take me back on
the special train

04:43:16.000 --> 04:43:17.860
to the glorious institute.

04:43:17.860 --> 04:43:21.350
I yearn for the inspiration
of the technological toot.

04:43:21.350 --> 04:43:24.035
I'd shun the quizzical
physical profs, the chapel,

04:43:24.035 --> 04:43:26.924
and all that, but how
I'd love to go again

04:43:26.924 --> 04:43:28.671
on a scientific bat.

04:43:28.671 --> 04:43:31.907
La, la, la, la, la, la, la, la,
la, la, la, la, la, la, la, la,

04:43:31.907 --> 04:43:34.532
la, la, la, la, la, la, la, la,
la, la, la, la, la, la, la, la,

04:43:34.532 --> 04:43:35.864
la, la, la, la, la, la, la, la.

04:43:35.864 --> 04:43:36.655
Do, do, do, do, do.

04:43:36.655 --> 04:43:37.652
La, la.

04:43:37.652 --> 04:43:38.152
Do, do.

04:43:38.152 --> 04:43:40.670
Da, da, da, da, da, da, da, da.

04:43:40.670 --> 04:43:49.076
Oh, M-A-S-S-A-C-H-U-S-E-T-T-S
I-N-S-T-I-T-U-T-E O-F T-E--

04:43:49.076 --> 04:43:49.850
and then it's--

04:43:49.850 --> 04:43:56.360
C-H-N-O-L-O-G and
Y comes after G.

04:43:56.360 --> 04:44:00.560
It's the Massachusetts
Institute of Technology.

04:44:00.560 --> 04:44:02.060
Hey!

04:44:02.060 --> 04:44:04.160
[CHEERS AND APPLAUSE]

04:44:09.560 --> 04:44:12.910
[MUSIC - MASS BRASS]

